original-numeric-contracts.json, original-numeric-512.json and the corresponding
remaining_numeric_contracts.rs cases are adapted from itpyi/magna at revision
56847478c840395735146ef1e1ccdc3d8aedc10f. Original sources:
- tests/core/test_native_proposals.py
- tests/core/test_simulator_optimization.py
- tests/core/test_noise_numeric_fastpaths.py
- tests/native/rational_random.cpp
- tests/support/decimal_estimator.py

Original repository: https://github.com/itpyi/magna
Full license: ../fixtures/original_many_record_input.LICENSE.
Producers: benchmarks/magna_reproduction/original_numeric_contracts.py and
benchmarks/magna_reproduction/original_numeric_512.py.

The first fixture executes five complete unchanged original methods and records
explicit range/bit protocols, exact input strings, Native Decimal results and
estimator exports. Nonfinite Native float exports are tagged strict JSON values.
The second retains all original standalone C++ assertions, adds observational
logging without additional RNG calls and checks all 512 pairs independently
using Python Fraction rounding. Native/helper/frontend/source/producer/compiler
identities are retained as applicable. Temporary standalone executables are
removed. Neither producer rebuilds the Native extension or copies an environment.

Rust checks explicit protocols and exact fields/statistics with scientific and
binary64 output. Python Random state representations and Decimal context/string
formatting are reference observations, not promised Rust interfaces.
